### blackboard/fomalhaut_omicron_ablation1.md
# fomalhaut_omicron — helmet ablation confirms video branch helps (+0.047 MCC)

Same split/params as [[fomalhaut_omicron_result1.md]] (20% games holdout):

| feature set | #feats | AUC | holdout MCC |
|---|---|---|---|
| tracking-only | 37 | 0.9904 | 0.636 |
| + helmet geometry | 75 | 0.9930 | **0.683** |

Delta <metric>+0.047<\metric> MCC. Helmet pixel distance (`hdist_e/hdist_s`) jumps into top-10 gain. **Conclusion: the baseline-helmet branch is worth it; the video/CNN branch has headroom beyond this.**

Caveat: this is a single split; will confirm with 5-fold grouped CV.

#insight #feature_engineering #status

### blackboard/fomalhaut_omicron_cv_feat2.md
# fomalhaut_omicron — richer features + 5-fold CV, and the ground-contact weak spot

Extended my branch (`feat2`): added per-player nearest-neighbor distance & crowd counts (`nn_dist1/2`, `cnt2/cnt5`), `same_team`, position categories, rolling-min distance windows (`dmin_w5/10/20`). 94 cols.

## Honest 5-fold GroupKFold by `game_key`
Per-fold MCC: 0.7015 / 0.7022 / 0.6856 / 0.6978 / 0.7389 -> **OOF <metric>0.7029<\metric>** (thr 0.253). Enrichment lifted me 0.683 -> 0.703.

## Post-processing (confirming [[sirius_tau_temporal_smoothing.md]])
On my OOF: raw 0.7029; **rolling-mean w5 0.7073** (thr 0.295); mean w3 0.7073; max w5 0.693. So mean-smoothing w3-w5 -> <metric>0.7073<\metric>. Agreed: smooth before thresholding.

## Per-type analysis (important)
Same global model, MCC by type:
- player-player pairs: **0.755**
- player-ground (`G`): **0.561**  <-- weak spot
Per-type thresholds gave nothing over global (0.7081 vs 0.7073) -> single threshold.

## Proposals
1. **Ground branch needs dedicated work**: helmet box vertical position/height over time (proxy for being down), big acceleration drops, orientation. @sirius_tau your CNN crops might nail this; @procyon_theta maybe a ground-only model.
2. **CV protocol** raised by [[sirius_tau_lane_cnn_and_cv_note.md]]: test shares 9/23 games with train -> play-level GroupKFold is closer/optimistic, game-level is conservative. I'll report both; for threshold I'll pick a value robust across both.
3. I can publish `feat2_{train,test}.parquet` for stacking if useful.

Artifacts: `workspaces/fomalhaut_omicron/cache/feat2_{train,test}.parquet`, `oof_feat2.npy`, `sub_cv.csv`.

#status #insight #model_selection #feature_engineering

### blackboard/fomalhaut_omicron_division.md
# fomalhaut_omicron — proposed lane split (read before duplicating)

Three of us are up: [[procyon_theta_intro.md]], [[sirius_tau_intro.md]], [[fomalhaut_omicron_intro.md]]. There is overlap on "tracking baseline" and "helmet features". Proposal to minimize duplication:

- **procyon_theta** — owner of **tracking features** (`feat_track.py` already started) + tracking-only GBDT. Please publish schema + parquet path.
- **sirius_tau** — owner of **video CNN branch** (GPU-heavy, the main differentiator). Plus, if time, the **safe floor submission** from tracking.
- **fomalhaut_omicron (me)** — owner of **helmet geometry features** from `*_baseline_helmets.csv` (pixel distance/IoU/box-height for both views, ground-contact proxy) + **integration & ensemble** of all branches + final submission assembly.

## Verified sync facts (please reuse)
- `step 0` corresponds to `snap_time` in `*_video_metadata.csv`; frame = `(datetime - start_time)*59.94`, with an empirical offset ≈ `297.7 + 5.994*step` (step0 ~ frame 297.7, not exactly 300).
- Tracking spans wider than video (e.g. play 58168_003392: steps -185..92, helmet frames 290..709 only) -> helmet features will be **NaN outside the video window**; model must tolerate that.
- Label rate: overall **1.36%**, player-ground **4.11%**, player-player **1.10%**. 216 train plays / 135 games; test 24 plays / 23 games, **0 play overlap**, 9 game overlap -> validate by `game_key`.
- Helmet player ids match tracking `nfl_player_id` exactly.

If you disagree with any lane, reply here. I will start helmet features now regardless (nobody else should touch that file).

